 "scope": "Home visibility check for planned-pose targets (CPU). A full-scene ray cast at the settled home pose (ground plane, orchard, both trees, the robot's render meshes, the visual jaw surrogate boxes, the runner's blender-mode wrist mount) applies the runner's own initialization rule: the depth at the seed pixel must be within 0.02 m of the expected optical Z. It explains the 3721 stop (its seed ray hits the ground 47 mm in front of the spur; the planner's line-of-sight model has no ground plane) and is validated on every recorded run with a recorded initialization. Exploratory: produced by scratch scripts (hashed below), not a committed tool; it is used here only to register predictions, which the October 6 sweep tests.",
